    "q-128961": {
      "dom_id": "step-q128961",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is the slope of the line $8x+2y=-7?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+2y & =-7 \\\\ 2y & =-8x-7 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & =\\frac{-8x-7}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{-8x}{2}-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ y & =-4x-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=-4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
