      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The slope of the line $2y-3=0$ is $m=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-3 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the line is horizontal, and its slope is $m=0.$",
